  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anupam Rajendra Gosvi vs The State Of Maharashtra on 22 July, 2025 1154.25aba (1) In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad 965 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1154 Of 2025 Anupam Rajendra Gosvi Versus The State Of Maharashtra ..... Mr A. J. Patil, Advocate for Applicant. Mr M. K. Goyanka, App for respondent/State. ..... Coram : Advait M. Sethna, J. Date : 22 July 2025",
    "facts": "The FIR is lodged on 06/06/2025 at 04:12 hours with the Muktai Nagar Police Station, Dist. Jalgaon. The offences are registered under Sections 26(2)(iv), 59, 27(3)(d), 27(3)(e), 3 of the Food Safety and Standards Act and under Sections 123, 223 and 274 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. 3. As far as allegations against present applicant is concerned it appears that his name is revealed during the investigation by accused No.1. Accused No.1 has specifically stated that this applicant is the seller of the alleged contraband.",
    "arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation."
